      },
      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${x}^{2}-10x+19.$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+19\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${5}^{2},$ writing the constant term $19$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2}}_{\u23df}-\\,{5}^{2}+19\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-5{)}^{2}-{5}^{2}+19\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x-5{)}^{2}-6.\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
